       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Most inpatient regimens stay at or below 2,400 mg/day. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, divided differently\n- **Something else.** If you really want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
